**Handle descriptor read failures as observation failures.**

If the returned run’s journal is corrupt or unreadable, `readKernelRunDescriptors` can throw at `src/ops/fix/runFix.ts:763`. The outer catch then returns a failed result before unit processing and PR assembly. `finish()` recovers collected tasks, but not the skipped unit processing or original verdict.

<details>
<summary>Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
-      const descriptors =
-        input.journalDir === undefined
-          ? []
-          : await readKernelRunDescriptors(journalDir, [report.run.runId]);
+      let descriptors: KernelRunDescriptor[] = [];
+      if (input.journalDir !== undefined) {
+        try {
+          descriptors = await readKernelRunDescriptors(journalDir, [report.run.runId]);
+        } catch (error) {
+          observationFailure(error);
+        }
+      }
```
</details>
